      "id": 1,
      "text": "Herald Harbor’s name comes from the Washington Herald newspaper, which once gave away small plots of land for summer homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herald_Harbor%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, special excursion trains ran from Washington, D.C., to a station near Herald Harbor, where motor buses ferried passengers to the Severn River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heraldharbor.org/history",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Long Point on the Severn River, a stretch of Herald Harbor, is known for its affluent, retired residents and scenic waterfront views.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herald_Harbor%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Herald Harbor offers a quiet residential feel with sweeping views of the Severn River, just a short drive from Crownsville and Interstate 97.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herald_Harbor%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "An old brick mansion in Herald Harbor once served as a country club, inn, and Dutch Tea Room before closing its doors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heraldharbor.org/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
